WEBVTT

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.633
Torres to Voyager.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.634
I could use a little help here.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.799
What's your status?

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.433
I'm approaching your position,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.637
but that ion storm
blew out my deflector field.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.203
I've lost helm control,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.045
and I'm venting plasma
from the port nacelle.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.518
We're modifying a tractor pulse
to slow you down.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.214
Acknowledged.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.778
The arresting fields
are in place.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.789
You're clear to land.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.950
Hold on, B'Elanna.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.050
This is going to be bumpy.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.232
B'Elanna?

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.209
Oh.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.540
Are you alive?

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.241
You tell me.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.613
You've got a mild concussion.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.249
That's the best thing
that's happened to me all day.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.353
When I give you an order,
I expect you to follow it.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.922
I told you to return to Voyager,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.932
not chase the probe

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.935
into the center
of an ion storm.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.493
We only have one
multispatial probe.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.799
I didn't want to lose it.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.533
We only have
one B'Elanna Torres.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.302
I don't want to lose her,
either.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.936
Understood.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.479
Lanna...

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.711
I'm glad you made it back
in one piece.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.274
Did you just call me "Lanna"?

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.945
I suppose I did.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.218
That's what my mother
used to call me.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.954
Well, then, I'm in good company.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.028
Come in.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.905
Feeling better?

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.138
I've felt worse.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.738
I found something you might
be interested in.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.545
It's what my ancestors called
a "monkey wrench."

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.586
It was lodged
in your port nacelle.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.245
How did it get there?

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:05.587
Judging by your sensor logs,
it looks like you ran into it

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.717
after your deflector field
collapsed.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.025
But the big question is:
How did it get in this quadrant?

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:14.089
What do you mean?

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.101
What?

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.431
It's Klingon.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.732
And it's old.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.238
That's about all we know.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.764
Looks like the Klingons beat
Starfleet to the Delta Quadrant

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.208
by a few hundred years.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:28.577
You may be holding the most
important archaeological find

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.945
in Klingon history.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.052
Remind me to plant a flag
on behalf of the Empire.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.349
You know, the simplest
explanation

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.322
is that the Borg assimilated
a bird-of-prey

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.450
somewhere in the Alpha Quadrant,

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:43.860
and they blew it out an airlock
on their way home.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.454
Maybe so.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:49.730
In any case, it makes
a nice souvenir.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:25.488
Harry, it bled, it screamed.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.116
There's got to be
some explanation.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.353
Hey, I've got one for you.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.396
You hit your head harder
than you thought.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.896
I wasn't hallucinating.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.159
Now, run a submolecular scan.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.360
How many more scans
are we going to run?

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.267
There is nothing there.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.568
No fluid or vapor residue.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.700
We may find some irregularities
at the atomic level.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.744
It's a hunk of metal.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.746
What you heard
may have had nothing to do

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.076
with this artifact.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.740
Maybe the com system

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.478
picked up some stray
signal from a pulsar...

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.484
I don't know.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.418
A pulsar that speaks Klingon.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:59.151
Okay, B'Elanna, there
probably is some explanation

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.023
for what happened,
but it's 0300 hours.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:04.427
I'm tired, you're tired.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.727
Let's just stick this thing
in a containment field

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.460
and deal with it in the morning.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.058
Ah! Just the daughter

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:12.434
of the Empire
I've been looking for.

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.905
I wanted to be the first
to congratulate you

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.272
on your discovery
of the Klingon artifact.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.311
Neelix, I ran into it
with a shuttle.

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:22.041
Some of the greatest discoveries
in Klingon history

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.446
were accidents.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:26.576
When Sarpek the Fearless
unearthed the Knife of Kiromm

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.779
he was searching
for his lost targ.

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.914
Isn't that amazing?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.423
I've been doing some research.

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:33.481
Why?

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:35.117
Well, I'm planning
a celebration.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.855
This... must be the treasure.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.760
Neelix, look, I appreciate
your enthusiasm,

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:40.059
but since I'm the only
Klingon onboard,

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.600
there's really no point
in throwing a party.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.929
Oh, nonsense.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.936
This artifact isn't just
a testament to Klingon spirit.

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:48.267
It's a piece
of the Alpha Quadrant...

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.571
a symbol of Voyager's home,

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.873
and that's just as worthy
of celebration and song

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.537
as finding some old knife.

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:56.206
Man's got a point.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.271
Besides, I've already

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.147
replicated five barrels
of bloodwine.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.617
I'm not going to let them
go to waste.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.210
Festivities begin
at 1900 hours.

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:05.155
Oh! Uh, I almost forgot.

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.089
As guest of honor,
you're gonna be expected

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.151
to say a few words
on behalf of your people.

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:12.888
Sounds like you got
a big day ahead of you.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.194
You should probably
get some rest.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.661
All right, all right,
let's call it a night.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:20.831
Thank you.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:27.205
Do not underestimate
the power of the mind.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.875
The artifact was a catalyst for
your already active imagination.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:34.681
It served as an unwelcome
reminder of your ancestry...

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.346
the self-loathing you experience

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:39.653
when you look in the mirror
and see a Klingon.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.920
Who said anything
about self-loathing?

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.655
You despise being Klingon.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.287
It's no secret.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.195
What you experienced
in your quarters

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:51.498
was a subconscious manifestation
of that hatred.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:57.373
The blood in your veins,
the voices of your ancestors...

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:59.741
all symbols
of your Klingon heritage.

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.576
And when the blood
disappeared,

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:03.808
that was, what?

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:07.250
Me trying to vaporize
that part of myself?

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.117
Yes.

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:13.557
But the essence of who you are...
the artifact itself... remained.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.423
And the moral of the story
is?

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.861
Quite simple.
That despite your efforts

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.693
to become something else,

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:22.256
whether it be Starfleet
or Maquis,

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:25.429
your Klingon nature
continues to assert itself.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.700
That's an intriguing theory.

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.435
Perhaps we should forego
your meditation

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.637
in favor
of a different exercise.

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.737
Fine by me.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.613
This should be interesting.

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:42.677
Feel the weight of the bat'leth
in your hands.

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:50.793
Describe the first thought
that enters your mind.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:54.765
It's a clumsy weapon,
overstated,

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.200
like everything else Klingon.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.738
You can't see the elegance
of its design,

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.239
because of your hatred.

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:05.141
I don't hate Klingons.

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.042
It's a warrior's blade...

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.978
crafted for precision

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.208
and balance.

00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:11.250
Observe.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:32.002
Is this your idea of therapy?!

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.471
Listen to yourself whine
like a Ferengi.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.632
Pahtk!

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.835
You're not worthy
of the blood in your veins.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.811
A true Klingon would try
to kill me where I stand.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.313
What the hell
has gotten into you?

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:45.282
This exercise is over.

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.751
You are dismissed, Lieutenant,

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.119
and take your dishonor
with you.

00:09:57.263 --> 00:10:01.199
... migh hohk-chew koo

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:05.169
Ej IM-ta fe DE-ja i...

00:10:05.237 --> 00:10:08.172
And the blood was ankle-deep.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:11.767
Ejdahk-so-TAS ghos
va Skral byteek...

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.574
And the river Skral
ran crimson red.

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:15.671
I fail to see the merit

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.375
of learning a Klingon
drinking song.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.247
It's not about drinking, Seven.

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:22.845
It's about saluting the noble
deeds of our ancestors

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:25.755
and honoring those
who fell in battle.

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:27.952
Think "Qapla'!"

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:30.825
Think "Long live
the Empire!"

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.124
Think again.

00:10:32.198 --> 00:10:33.825
Okay, so I'm overdoing it a bit,

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.833
but try to get into the
spirit of the occasion.

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:38.335
Very well.

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:39.962
Ej IM-ta fey

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:41.939
DE-ja i

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:45.808
ejdahk-so-TAS
ghos va Skral byteek

00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:48.608
Empa jaj law-moch jaj-pusH

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:56.520
jaj Kahless Molor-migh
hohk-chew koo.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.280
Gagh, anyone?

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:01.918
Sop joq jiH yuv gagh drek!

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:03.621
He said, "Eat this

00:11:03.696 --> 00:11:06.221
or he'll force it down
the gullet of your corpse."

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:07.230
No offense.

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:08.732
Oh, none taken.

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:11.929
So this is replicated,
right?

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.028
Unfortunately.

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:17.371
And how do you get it to...
move?

00:11:17.443 --> 00:11:20.606
I used a kinesthetic agent
to give it a little oomph.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:25.808
Is it just me,

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:28.581
or has everyone
gone Klingon-happy?

00:11:28.654 --> 00:11:29.951
Oh, come on, B'Elanna.

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:31.819
They're all doing this for you.

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:34.223
Well, then they don't
know me very well.

00:11:34.293 --> 00:11:36.386
And if you even think
of joining in

00:11:36.462 --> 00:11:38.123
on this "embrace your heritage"
nonsense,

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:41.223
I swear I'll rip out your tongue
and wear it as a belt.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.100
Oh, no... there's not
a lot of Klingon in you.

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:49.733
I inherited the forehead and
the bad attitude... that's it.

00:11:55.648 --> 00:11:57.343
She would have loved all this.

00:11:57.416 --> 00:11:58.815
Your mother?

00:11:59.919 --> 00:12:03.514
She was so obsessed
with Klingon ritual, myths.

00:12:03.589 --> 00:12:06.456
It used to drive
my father and me crazy.

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:11.087
Did I ever tell you that she
put me in a Klingon monastery?

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.926
Ah. You're kidding.

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.191
It was after their marriage
ended.

00:12:14.266 --> 00:12:15.665
She pulled me
out of the Federation school

00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:20.138
in order to teach me...
honor and discipline.

00:12:20.206 --> 00:12:24.267
Hmm... out of the plasma cooker
into the fire.

00:12:24.343 --> 00:12:25.640
She prayed to Kahless every day

00:12:25.711 --> 00:12:27.338
to guide me in the ways
of the warrior.

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:28.937
I guess he wasn't listening.

00:12:30.683 --> 00:12:33.846
Ladies and gentlemen, could I
have your attention, please?

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:35.648
I hate to interrupt
the festivities,

00:12:35.721 --> 00:12:38.815
but before I turn the floor
over to our resident Klingon,

00:12:38.891 --> 00:12:42.622
I'd like to say a few words.

00:12:42.695 --> 00:12:44.720
This is a great day
for the Klingon Empire...

00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:47.698
a day when we honor
their ancestors.

00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:53.831
Those warriors whose deeds
of valor and glory...

00:12:53.906 --> 00:12:56.466
led them to the Delta Quadrant.

00:12:56.542 --> 00:13:03.914
May they live on
in song and story.

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:36.173
Captain!

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.823
Legh soH va Gre'thor!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.779
Where am I?

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:14.376
Silence.

00:14:14.453 --> 00:14:17.752
The dead ask no questions.

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:30.794
Computer, end program!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.804
Qem nuH meq!

00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:34.464
Let go of me!

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:42.139
Wait... wait...

00:14:42.214 --> 00:14:43.306
'uch ghaH.

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:44.974
Uh, wait...

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.490
She won't take the mark.

00:14:57.897 --> 00:14:59.956
What the hell is going on?

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:00.861
Qusdaq.

00:15:00.933 --> 00:15:01.957
Ba'daH.

00:15:03.369 --> 00:15:05.496
Mag hoshonaH nes'a.

00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:07.038
Where am I?

00:15:07.106 --> 00:15:10.872
You should know;
you're half Klingon.

00:15:12.678 --> 00:15:14.339
Enlighten me.

00:15:16.515 --> 00:15:18.745
This is the Barge of the Dead.

00:15:18.817 --> 00:15:22.844
Our dishonored souls are
being taken to Gre'thor.

00:15:22.922 --> 00:15:24.890
Klingon hell is a myth.

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:27.016
That's what I thought...

00:15:27.092 --> 00:15:30.084
just a foolish superstition.

00:15:30.162 --> 00:15:32.323
Imagine my surprise.

00:15:34.934 --> 00:15:37.232
But I was on Voyager
with my crew.

00:15:37.303 --> 00:15:38.930
That was the naj...

00:15:39.038 --> 00:15:42.735
the dream before dying.

00:15:42.808 --> 00:15:44.935
When we can't accept
that we've died,

00:15:45.077 --> 00:15:47.045
we create the illusion of life

00:15:47.112 --> 00:15:49.080
to hold on to.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:56.954
He slaughtered my friends.

00:15:57.022 --> 00:16:00.890
No. He slaughtered the dream.

00:16:03.128 --> 00:16:06.222
He dragged you
from the illusion of life.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.230
This is where you belong.

00:16:18.777 --> 00:16:20.904
What is that?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.107
It's the kos'kari.

00:16:23.182 --> 00:16:27.016
They'll try to lure you to them.
Don't listen.

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:31.646
B'Elanna, are you there?

00:16:31.724 --> 00:16:33.316
Lieutenant, can you hear me?

00:16:33.392 --> 00:16:34.381
Help us find you!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.928
Tom? Chakotay?

00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:38.691
It's not your friends!

00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:41.599
JiH qoy soH!

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:59.648
There are things here
worse than death.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:02.482
You.

00:17:13.065 --> 00:17:15.590
Is this the mongrel
child you spoke of?

00:17:15.667 --> 00:17:18.329
Yes. The one whose face
would not bear the mark.

00:17:22.641 --> 00:17:27.738
B'Elanna, daughter of Miral...

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:29.781
it's not your time.

00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:31.577
How do you know my name?

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.117
You've come close

00:17:33.185 --> 00:17:35.619
to boarding this ship
many times.

00:17:35.687 --> 00:17:38.349
I remember the first.

00:17:38.424 --> 00:17:40.415
You were a child.

00:17:40.492 --> 00:17:43.427
Your mother took you
to the Sea of Gatan.

00:17:43.495 --> 00:17:47.022
Your curiosity was as deep
as the water.

00:17:47.099 --> 00:17:48.896
I fell in.

00:17:48.967 --> 00:17:50.935
I almost drowned.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.937
When your mother breathed life
back into your lungs

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:55.633
she told you about me.

00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:58.505
So you're supposed to be Kortar.

00:17:58.577 --> 00:18:02.104
Ah... you remember me.

00:18:02.181 --> 00:18:06.277
I remember the myth of Kortar,
the first Klingon.

00:18:06.351 --> 00:18:08.683
He destroyed the gods
who created him.

00:18:08.754 --> 00:18:11.848
And as punishment,
I was condemned to ferry

00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:15.189
the souls of the dishonored
to Gre'thor.

00:18:19.465 --> 00:18:24.732
I may have believed in you
as a child, but not anymore.

00:18:24.803 --> 00:18:29.035
If you didn't still believe,
you wouldn't be here.

00:18:34.012 --> 00:18:35.479
Foolish girl.

00:18:38.283 --> 00:18:40.376
You cannot harm me.

00:18:40.452 --> 00:18:42.420
I'm already dead.

00:18:55.701 --> 00:18:57.896
What's happening?

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:02.566
The soul of another dishonored
warrior is being delivered.

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:07.202
Kot'mah soH Gre'thor!

00:19:07.279 --> 00:19:08.337
Qapla.

00:19:13.986 --> 00:19:15.419
Mother.

00:19:19.992 --> 00:19:21.892
It's all right.

00:19:21.994 --> 00:19:23.894
You're safe.

00:19:29.701 --> 00:19:30.827
Your shuttle was drifting

00:19:30.903 --> 00:19:32.165
on the trailing edge
of an ion storm.

00:19:32.237 --> 00:19:33.261
You lost life support.

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:34.862
We found you just in time.

00:19:38.977 --> 00:19:41.411
But I got through the storm.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.847
I remember
crashing into the Shuttle Bay.

00:19:44.917 --> 00:19:48.045
When we tractored your
shuttle back to Voyager,

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.553
you were in a coma.

00:19:49.621 --> 00:19:51.282
We almost lost you.

00:19:54.793 --> 00:19:56.727
The Klingon artifact...

00:19:56.795 --> 00:19:58.057
Artifact?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.797
My hand...

00:20:07.005 --> 00:20:09.906
You took quite
a beating out there...

00:20:09.975 --> 00:20:13.809
more than your fair share
of cuts and bruises.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.157
Come in.

00:20:37.736 --> 00:20:39.704
How are you feeling?

00:20:39.771 --> 00:20:42.672
Um... a little out of place.

00:20:42.741 --> 00:20:44.140
Would you like to talk about it?

00:20:44.209 --> 00:20:45.801
Yes...

00:20:45.877 --> 00:20:48.175
and no.

00:20:50.182 --> 00:20:52.116
Let me know when you decide.

00:20:52.184 --> 00:20:55.813
I don't know how to say this
without sounding crazy.

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.457
Try.

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:09.930
Do you believe in an afterlife?

00:21:10.002 --> 00:21:12.664
I accept there are
things in the universe

00:21:12.738 --> 00:21:15.298
than can't be scanned
with a tricorder.

00:21:16.975 --> 00:21:18.636
What happened to you out there?

00:21:20.846 --> 00:21:22.313
I think...

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:24.915
I died.

00:21:24.983 --> 00:21:28.077
I died, and I was on
the Barge of the Dead,

00:21:28.153 --> 00:21:29.950
in the Klingon afterlife.

00:21:30.022 --> 00:21:32.217
Klingon mythology has
been ingrained in you

00:21:32.291 --> 00:21:33.553
since you were a child.

00:21:33.625 --> 00:21:35.684
It's not surprising
you experienced some

00:21:35.761 --> 00:21:37.956
of those images while
you were unconscious.

00:21:38.096 --> 00:21:41.259
I saw my mother, Chakotay.

00:21:41.333 --> 00:21:45.292
If it was real, then she's dead.

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:46.837
B'Elanna...

00:21:46.905 --> 00:21:49.339
your mother...
the Barge of the Dead...

00:21:49.408 --> 00:21:52.309
these are just symbols.

00:21:52.377 --> 00:21:54.607
It's your subconscious mind
trying to tell you something.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.942
Tell me what?

00:21:56.014 --> 00:21:57.914
That my mother is going to hell?

00:21:57.983 --> 00:22:00.451
You need time
to digest what you experienced.

00:22:00.519 --> 00:22:02.282
You have to interpret
the symbols

00:22:02.354 --> 00:22:03.912
and search for their meaning.

00:22:03.989 --> 00:22:07.220
What if there is no symbolism
to interpret?

00:22:07.292 --> 00:22:09.590
What if the afterlife is real?

00:22:09.661 --> 00:22:11.925
I'm an engineer.

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:14.430
My whole life,
I've immersed myself

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:16.763
in science and...
and schematics.

00:22:16.835 --> 00:22:20.362
But what if it's time
to start looking beyond that?

00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:26.102
My grandfather used to...

00:22:26.178 --> 00:22:28.772
think he could transform himself
into a wolf,

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:32.305
so that he could venture out
to explore the spirit realm.

00:22:32.384 --> 00:22:34.284
It was real to him.

00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:37.288
As real as what you experienced
was to you,

00:22:37.356 --> 00:22:40.951
but that doesn't mean
he grew hair all over his body

00:22:41.059 --> 00:22:43.027
and walked around on all fours.

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:54.904
My mother has been
on my mind a lot lately.

00:22:54.973 --> 00:22:58.067
We just had a big anniversary.

00:22:58.143 --> 00:22:59.940
It's been ten years...

00:23:00.979 --> 00:23:02.947
since we talked.

00:23:05.484 --> 00:23:08.578
But it was so real.

00:23:08.653 --> 00:23:12.419
I could taste the blood
in the air.

00:23:12.491 --> 00:23:15.927
I could feel the wind.

00:23:15.994 --> 00:23:19.259
I was seasick
from the rocking of the boat.

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:31.834
Hi.

00:23:32.511 --> 00:23:34.411
Hi.

00:23:34.479 --> 00:23:36.413
What are you reading?

00:23:36.481 --> 00:23:37.743
The paq'batlh.

00:23:37.816 --> 00:23:40.580
It's a sacred Klingon scroll.

00:23:40.652 --> 00:23:42.244
Find anything?

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:45.414
You don't want to know.

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:46.616
Oh, come on.

00:23:46.691 --> 00:23:47.851
It can't be that bad.

00:23:47.926 --> 00:23:49.325
You want to bet?

00:23:50.695 --> 00:23:54.859
I found out why my mother
is on her way to Gre'thor.

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:57.401
It's because I sent her there.

00:23:57.469 --> 00:24:00.233
What do you mean?

00:24:00.305 --> 00:24:01.636
The sins of the child.

00:24:01.706 --> 00:24:05.642
She's being punished
for my dishonor.

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:08.178
I turned my back
on everything Klingon,

00:24:08.246 --> 00:24:10.407
and now she has
to pay the price.

00:24:10.482 --> 00:24:12.541
B'Elanna, you can't even be sure

00:24:12.617 --> 00:24:15.586
your mother is dead,
much less blame yourself

00:24:15.654 --> 00:24:18.418
for what happens to her
in some afterlife.

00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:20.424
Look at this.

00:24:20.492 --> 00:24:23.017
The Eleventh Tome of Klavek.

00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:26.427
It's a story about Kahless
returning from the dead...

00:24:26.498 --> 00:24:28.693
"still bearing a wound
from the afterlife"...

00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:31.327
a warning that what
he experienced wasn't a dream.

00:24:31.403 --> 00:24:32.927
The same thing happened to me.

00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:33.936
B'Elanna, this...

00:24:34.005 --> 00:24:34.937
And the only reason

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:36.940
Kahless was in the afterlife
to begin with

00:24:37.008 --> 00:24:39.033
was to rescue his brother
from the Barge of the Dead

00:24:39.110 --> 00:24:39.940
and deliver him to Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:24:40.078 --> 00:24:41.102
Okay.

00:24:41.179 --> 00:24:42.407
Don't you see?

00:24:42.481 --> 00:24:45.177
I have a chance
to rescue my mother

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:48.913
if I can accept responsibility
for her dishonor

00:24:48.987 --> 00:24:52.787
before she passes through
the gates of Gre'thor.

00:24:52.858 --> 00:24:54.382
I have to go back.

00:24:56.328 --> 00:24:57.386
Whoa. Wait a minute.

00:24:57.462 --> 00:24:58.952
What do you mean, "go back"?

00:24:59.030 --> 00:25:01.498
I can't let her suffer
for what I've done.

00:25:03.635 --> 00:25:05.569
It's the only way.

00:25:05.637 --> 00:25:09.903
B'Elanna, I respect
what you believe in,

00:25:10.041 --> 00:25:13.568
but you're starting to scare me.

00:25:13.645 --> 00:25:15.613
I'm scaring myself.

00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:20.178
It's a controlled procedure.

00:25:20.252 --> 00:25:21.913
I'll be under
constant supervision.

00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:24.784
The Doctor can simulate
the conditions of the ion storm.

00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:27.552
He's agreed to help me,
but only with your permission.

00:25:27.626 --> 00:25:30.561
I'm still not inclined
to grant your request.

00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:32.597
Are you telling me

00:25:32.664 --> 00:25:34.928
that I can't pursue
my spiritual beliefs?

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:36.126
B'Elanna,
I'm not going to let you

00:25:36.201 --> 00:25:37.930
turn this into a debate
about freedom of worship.

00:25:38.003 --> 00:25:39.163
But that's what it is.

00:25:40.238 --> 00:25:41.899
There's a limit to how far

00:25:41.973 --> 00:25:45.101
I'll let religious practices go
aboard this ship.

00:25:45.176 --> 00:25:46.905
If your belief system
required you

00:25:46.978 --> 00:25:48.673
to sacrifice a child
to your gods,

00:25:48.747 --> 00:25:50.271
I wouldn't allow that, either.

00:25:50.348 --> 00:25:51.610
That's an absurd example.

00:25:51.683 --> 00:25:54.311
You want to simulate
a near-death experience,

00:25:54.386 --> 00:25:56.718
so you can revisit
the Barge of Death,

00:25:56.788 --> 00:25:59.222
and you're telling me
what's absurd?

00:25:59.291 --> 00:26:00.724
Bottom line, B'Elanna...

00:26:00.792 --> 00:26:03.192
I'm not going to let you
risk your life for this.

00:26:03.261 --> 00:26:04.489
Captain, please.

00:26:04.563 --> 00:26:06.030
Request denied.

00:26:07.098 --> 00:26:09.658
What I do with my own life
is one thing,

00:26:09.734 --> 00:26:12.601
but to know that I have
condemned my mother...

00:26:12.671 --> 00:26:14.036
that because of what I've done,
she's...

00:26:14.105 --> 00:26:16.573
I appreciate what you're
trying to say, B'Elanna,

00:26:16.641 --> 00:26:19.269
but whatever you experienced,
it wasn't real.

00:26:19.344 --> 00:26:21.244
It doesn't matter
if you think it was real.

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:22.610
It was real to me.

00:26:27.485 --> 00:26:31.751
Whatever it was, it changed me.

00:26:31.823 --> 00:26:33.586
I can't ignore that.

00:26:33.658 --> 00:26:36.058
I need to confront
what's happened.

00:26:38.330 --> 00:26:40.457
I'm sorry.

00:26:42.100 --> 00:26:44.068
You know, you're just like her.

00:26:44.135 --> 00:26:45.227
Lieutenant?

00:26:45.303 --> 00:26:47.271
My mother.

00:26:47.339 --> 00:26:49.637
You're as dedicated
to Starfleet principles

00:26:49.708 --> 00:26:51.972
as she was to Klingon honor.

00:26:53.044 --> 00:26:56.480
I know that we haven't
always seen eye to eye,

00:26:56.548 --> 00:26:58.311
but despite our differences,

00:26:58.383 --> 00:27:00.578
you helped me
become a good officer

00:27:00.652 --> 00:27:02.813
and I'd like to think
that you're proud of me for it.

00:27:02.887 --> 00:27:04.320
I am.

00:27:05.423 --> 00:27:10.759
My mother never had the chance
to be proud of me.

00:27:10.829 --> 00:27:13.730
I'd like her to know me
the way you do.

00:27:20.238 --> 00:27:25.676
I don't want her to die
thinking of me as a disgrace.

00:27:25.744 --> 00:27:29.009
You have to let me do this.

00:27:31.616 --> 00:27:35.416
I can't believe the Captain
is allowing this.

00:27:35.487 --> 00:27:36.920
One minute, you're in a coma.

00:27:36.988 --> 00:27:39.081
The next, you're
a born-again Klingon?

00:27:39.157 --> 00:27:40.419
I-I just don't get it.

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:41.857
I'm not sure I get it, either.

00:27:41.926 --> 00:27:43.860
I just know this is something
I have to do.

00:27:43.928 --> 00:27:45.190
There's got to be an easier way

00:27:45.263 --> 00:27:47.060
for you to explore
your spirituality.

00:27:47.132 --> 00:27:49.100
Go to church, or something?

00:27:49.167 --> 00:27:50.725
It wouldn't be enough.

00:27:50.802 --> 00:27:52.770
Look, I'll read the scrolls.

00:27:52.837 --> 00:27:54.236
I'll learn Klingon.

00:27:54.305 --> 00:27:56.432
We'll figure this out...
together.

00:27:56.508 --> 00:27:58.738
Next time.

00:28:00.945 --> 00:28:03.379
I just hope
there is a next time.

00:28:03.448 --> 00:28:06.110
There will be.

00:28:08.953 --> 00:28:10.386
Report.

00:28:10.455 --> 00:28:11.888
I've examined the sensor logs

00:28:11.956 --> 00:28:13.389
from the shuttle mission.

00:28:13.458 --> 00:28:15.653
I should be able to re-create
the exact conditions

00:28:15.727 --> 00:28:17.558
that triggered
her near-death experience.

00:28:17.629 --> 00:28:19.597
Good. B'Elanna?

00:28:19.664 --> 00:28:21.393
I'm ready.

00:28:25.303 --> 00:28:26.770
Be careful.

00:28:35.580 --> 00:28:38.708
You'll have an hour to do
whatever it is you need to do.

00:28:38.783 --> 00:28:40.876
At the first sign of trouble,
we're bringing you out.

00:28:40.952 --> 00:28:41.919
Understood?

00:28:51.362 --> 00:28:53.091
Computer...

00:28:53.164 --> 00:28:56.361
erect an isolation field
around the Surgical Bay.

00:28:56.434 --> 00:28:58.368
Decrease oxygen concentration

00:28:58.436 --> 00:29:00.870
within the force field
by 27 percent.

00:29:00.939 --> 00:29:04.602
Begin ionizing
the enclosed atmosphere

00:29:04.676 --> 00:29:06.906
to 5,000 particles
per cubic meter.

00:29:10.515 --> 00:29:11.539
She's unconscious.

00:29:11.616 --> 00:29:12.878
Neural activity

00:29:12.951 --> 00:29:15.886
is decreasing to 87 percent...

00:29:15.954 --> 00:29:17.512
62 percent...

00:29:20.825 --> 00:29:22.224
Synaptic function is failing.

00:29:22.293 --> 00:29:24.227
Compensating.

00:29:25.296 --> 00:29:26.729
Neural activity is nominal.

00:29:26.798 --> 00:29:28.026
She's not breathing.

00:29:28.099 --> 00:29:29.327
She's still alive.

00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:31.334
Her lungs are taking in
just enough oxygen

00:29:31.402 --> 00:29:33.029
to keep her brain
from necrotizing.

00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:40.972
Qapla', B'Elanna.

00:30:24.022 --> 00:30:26.650
SuS'ag Gre'thor qay.

00:31:01.259 --> 00:31:02.226
Mother.

00:31:04.495 --> 00:31:05.723
Stay away.

00:31:05.797 --> 00:31:07.822
You are an illusion.

00:31:07.899 --> 00:31:09.890
You're a kos'kari
trying to lure me away.

00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:12.129
Mother, it's me.

00:31:13.171 --> 00:31:14.297
It's me.

00:31:15.473 --> 00:31:17.737
B'Elanna?

00:31:17.809 --> 00:31:18.969
No.

00:31:21.880 --> 00:31:23.609
Then you died as well?

00:31:23.681 --> 00:31:26.309
I've come to lift your dishonor.

00:31:26.384 --> 00:31:29.182
But you don't believe
in Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:31:29.254 --> 00:31:32.655
A lot's happened since
the last time I saw you.

00:31:32.724 --> 00:31:34.191
I've changed.

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:37.285
Not enough.

00:31:37.362 --> 00:31:42.129
It was you who brought
this damnation upon me.

00:31:44.369 --> 00:31:46.394
If you hadn't
tried to, to force me

00:31:46.471 --> 00:31:47.961
to become a warrior...

00:31:48.106 --> 00:31:51.269
I tried to guide you
in the ways of a Klingon.

00:31:51.342 --> 00:31:52.934
You tried a little too hard.

00:31:53.011 --> 00:31:55.878
If you had listened to me
when you were younger,

00:31:55.947 --> 00:31:57.938
we wouldn't be
on the Barge of the Dead.

00:31:58.016 --> 00:32:01.179
You were always running away.

00:32:01.252 --> 00:32:03.117
You drove me away...

00:32:03.187 --> 00:32:07.283
the same way you
drove away my father.

00:32:07.358 --> 00:32:10.919
He abandoned us.

00:32:11.062 --> 00:32:13.189
You pushed him to the point
where he couldn't bear

00:32:13.264 --> 00:32:17.394
to be around anything
Klingon... including me.

00:32:17.468 --> 00:32:21.461
I wanted to give you honor.

00:32:21.539 --> 00:32:23.939
And if you had understood that,

00:32:24.008 --> 00:32:28.502
I would not be
on my way to Gre'thor.

00:32:31.816 --> 00:32:34.080
We're on the Barge
of the Dead...

00:32:34.152 --> 00:32:36.882
and we're still having
the same argument

00:32:36.955 --> 00:32:38.889
we were having ten years ago.

00:32:40.358 --> 00:32:47.958
Look, if I have dishonored you,
I am truly sorry.

00:32:48.032 --> 00:32:49.260
Are you?

00:32:49.334 --> 00:32:52.303
You have too much anger
in your heart to be sorry.

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:53.928
Oh, we don't have
time for this

00:32:54.005 --> 00:32:56.496
if we're going to perform
the transference.

00:32:56.574 --> 00:32:58.974
Is that how you intend
to lift my dishonor?

00:32:59.077 --> 00:33:00.510
By taking my place?

00:33:00.578 --> 00:33:01.510
Oh, don't worry.

00:33:01.579 --> 00:33:04.070
I have no intention
of being on this barge

00:33:04.148 --> 00:33:05.672
when it gets to Gre'thor.

00:33:05.750 --> 00:33:08.218
We've got just enough time
to perform the ritual

00:33:08.286 --> 00:33:09.878
before my crew
resuscitates me.

00:33:09.954 --> 00:33:12.149
Oh.

00:33:12.223 --> 00:33:15.886
I should have known
you'd choose the easy way.

00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:18.155
What are you talking about?

00:33:18.229 --> 00:33:22.029
Do you know the risks
I've taken to save you?

00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:25.934
You still understand nothing
about being a Klingon.

00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:28.302
I would rather face damnation

00:33:28.373 --> 00:33:31.308
with what little honor
you have left me

00:33:31.376 --> 00:33:33.901
than cheat my way
into Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:33:42.520 --> 00:33:45.387
There she is.
Bring them.

00:33:49.193 --> 00:33:51.525
The mongrel child has returned.

00:33:51.596 --> 00:33:54.622
I'm here to take
my mother's place.

00:33:54.699 --> 00:33:55.825
B'Elanna!

00:33:55.900 --> 00:33:58.733
You wish to claim
her dishonor as your own?

00:33:58.803 --> 00:33:59.735
Yes.

00:33:59.804 --> 00:34:01.829
You're willing to die for her?

00:34:01.906 --> 00:34:03.168
Yes.
Release her to Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:34:03.241 --> 00:34:04.173
No!

00:34:04.242 --> 00:34:04.901
Keep her quiet!

00:34:05.009 --> 00:34:05.907
Silence!

00:34:06.010 --> 00:34:07.568
It's not your decision.

00:34:07.645 --> 00:34:10.671
She has the right
to reclaim your honor.

00:34:10.748 --> 00:34:12.340
Once we
have reached Gre'thor

00:34:12.417 --> 00:34:15.648
and you are within its gates,
I will release her.

00:34:15.720 --> 00:34:17.551
No. Now.

00:34:19.924 --> 00:34:22.893
You're very impatient.

00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:25.326
Time must be slipping away
in the living world.

00:34:25.396 --> 00:34:28.524
You're concerned that
your friends will revive you

00:34:28.599 --> 00:34:30.624
before you complete
your deception.

00:34:30.701 --> 00:34:33.636
Did you really think
I could be fooled so easily?

00:34:38.743 --> 00:34:40.142
I will die for her.

00:34:40.211 --> 00:34:42.145
No tricks,

00:34:42.213 --> 00:34:43.202
no games.

00:34:43.281 --> 00:34:46.546
I will take her place honorably.

00:34:48.653 --> 00:34:50.314
Like a Klingon.

00:34:50.388 --> 00:34:53.118
If you choose this path,

00:34:53.191 --> 00:34:55.352
your friends
will not be able to save you.

00:34:55.426 --> 00:34:57.951
No! I forbid it!

00:34:58.096 --> 00:35:00.064
I understand.

00:35:11.742 --> 00:35:13.573
Your dishonor has been lifted.

00:35:13.644 --> 00:35:14.906
Sto-Vo-Kor awaits you.

00:35:15.046 --> 00:35:18.015
I will not abandon my daughter.

00:35:18.082 --> 00:35:20.710
She has made the choice. Go!

00:35:31.262 --> 00:35:33.423
Daughter of Miral,

00:35:33.498 --> 00:35:36.058
embrace your fate.

00:35:49.514 --> 00:35:50.674
Vih.

00:36:06.097 --> 00:36:08.122
Her neural patterns
are breaking down.

00:36:08.199 --> 00:36:10.064
I'm initiating
emergency resuscitation.

00:36:10.134 --> 00:36:11.795
Vent the ionized particles.

00:36:30.388 --> 00:36:33.289
20 milligrams cordrazine now!

00:36:33.357 --> 00:36:35.257
I'm deactivating
the force field.

00:37:04.055 --> 00:37:06.717
Welcome to Gre'thor.

00:37:13.164 --> 00:37:14.825
This isn't Gre'thor.

00:37:14.899 --> 00:37:15.888
Oh, I assure you it is.

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:17.433
You've taken your mark.

00:37:19.637 --> 00:37:21.605
What is this,
some kind of a joke?

00:37:21.672 --> 00:37:24.505
This is no laughing matter.

00:37:24.575 --> 00:37:25.701
You've met Mr. Neelix,

00:37:25.776 --> 00:37:28.745
our Ambassador
to the recently deceased.

00:37:28.813 --> 00:37:32.340
Questions, comments,
suggestions... he's your man.

00:37:32.416 --> 00:37:33.610
If you'll follow me.

00:37:36.153 --> 00:37:37.814
By the way,
I'll be performing an aria

00:37:37.888 --> 00:37:38.820
from Berlioz's Faust

00:37:38.889 --> 00:37:40.914
tomorrow night in Holodeck 2.

00:37:41.058 --> 00:37:42.616
Feel free to stop by.

00:37:42.693 --> 00:37:44.923
15 decks.

00:37:45.029 --> 00:37:48.226
Computers augmented
with bio-neural circuitry.

00:37:48.299 --> 00:37:50.563
Top cruising speed:
Warp 9.975.

00:37:50.635 --> 00:37:52.933
Not that you'll
be going anywhere.

00:37:53.070 --> 00:37:54.901
No Fek'lhr?
No Cavern of Despair?

00:37:54.972 --> 00:37:55.939
Don't need them.

00:37:56.073 --> 00:37:58.439
I don't consider Voyager hell!

00:37:58.509 --> 00:37:59.533
Are you sure?

00:37:59.610 --> 00:38:01.737
Have you ever been
truly happy here?

00:38:01.812 --> 00:38:04.212
If you thought 50
years aboard this ship

00:38:04.282 --> 00:38:06.273
would be difficult,
try eternity.

00:38:07.985 --> 00:38:10.317
Ej IM-ta fey DE-ja i

00:38:10.388 --> 00:38:14.051
ejdahk-so-TAS
ghos va Skral byteek

00:38:14.125 --> 00:38:16.491
Empa jaj law-mooch
jaj-pusH...

00:38:17.595 --> 00:38:20.086
This is a great day
for B'Elanna Torres,

00:38:20.164 --> 00:38:23.429
a day when we pay tribute
to her dishonor.

00:38:23.501 --> 00:38:25.628
She's not responding
to the cordrazine.

00:38:25.703 --> 00:38:29.764
Neural activity
at 48 percent... 37.

00:38:29.840 --> 00:38:30.829
We're losing her.

00:38:30.908 --> 00:38:33.308
We have to stabilize
her synaptic functions.

00:38:33.377 --> 00:38:35.777
I'm attempting
a direct neural resequencing.

00:38:35.846 --> 00:38:38.781
B'Elanna's misdeeds
have led her to Gre'thor.

00:38:38.849 --> 00:38:41.340
She comes with no valor,
no glory...

00:38:41.419 --> 00:38:44.479
nothing to celebrate
in song and story.

00:38:44.555 --> 00:38:47.353
You really have no one
to blame but yourself.

00:38:47.425 --> 00:38:48.915
You've kept us all
at arm's length,

00:38:49.026 --> 00:38:50.926
even Tom, who you claim to love.

00:38:51.028 --> 00:38:52.154
Here, here.

00:38:52.229 --> 00:38:53.218
I tried to assist you

00:38:53.297 --> 00:38:54.821
in making Engineering
more efficient,

00:38:54.899 --> 00:38:57.026
but you resisted.
You're stubborn.

00:38:57.101 --> 00:38:59.661
She inherited that from her
mother along with the forehead.

00:38:59.737 --> 00:39:01.671
What do you think
of the afterlife so far?

00:39:01.739 --> 00:39:04.105
It's not exactly
what I had in mind.

00:39:04.175 --> 00:39:05.437
Are you interpreting
all the symbols?

00:39:05.509 --> 00:39:08.478
Searching your subconscious
for their meaning?

00:39:08.546 --> 00:39:10.036
Lieutenant Torres...

00:39:10.114 --> 00:39:11.945
defend yourself.

00:39:19.457 --> 00:39:21.084
Captain?

00:39:25.129 --> 00:39:27.256
What are you still doing here?

00:39:27.331 --> 00:39:29.629
I've released you to Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:32.168
You can't free me
until you free yourself.

00:39:32.236 --> 00:39:34.101
I don't understand.

00:39:34.171 --> 00:39:35.502
You never did.

00:39:35.573 --> 00:39:37.905
I did everything
that the ritual told me to do.

00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:39.168
I came back for you...

00:39:39.243 --> 00:39:40.733
Forget the ritual.

00:39:40.811 --> 00:39:42.278
It's meaningless.

00:39:42.346 --> 00:39:43.836
Meaningless?

00:39:43.914 --> 00:39:45.848
I died for you.

00:39:45.916 --> 00:39:47.247
No, you didn't.

00:39:47.318 --> 00:39:49.047
It's not your time.

00:39:49.120 --> 00:39:52.681
You still
don't understand this journey.

00:39:52.757 --> 00:39:54.315
Then tell me.

00:39:54.392 --> 00:39:56.917
Request denied.

00:39:56.994 --> 00:39:58.689
What do you want?

00:39:58.763 --> 00:40:00.526
Who are you asking?

00:40:00.598 --> 00:40:02.657
You, Kahless, the tooth fairy!

00:40:02.733 --> 00:40:06.169
Anybody who will tell me
what I am supposed to do!

00:40:06.237 --> 00:40:09.866
You are the only one
who can answer that question.

00:40:12.109 --> 00:40:15.374
Choose to live, B'Elanna.

00:40:20.885 --> 00:40:22.648
Neural activity's at 23 percent.

00:40:22.720 --> 00:40:25.348
Initiate cortical stimulation.

00:40:25.423 --> 00:40:27.618
Pulses at 50 millijoules.

00:40:27.691 --> 00:40:28.851
No effect.

00:40:28.926 --> 00:40:31.952
Increase to 70 millijoules.

00:40:32.096 --> 00:40:33.461
Come on, B'Elanna.

00:40:43.607 --> 00:40:45.541
Defend yourself.

00:40:47.545 --> 00:40:49.809
You want me to fight?

00:40:49.880 --> 00:40:52.815
You want me to be
a good little Klingon?

00:40:54.952 --> 00:40:56.442
Is that it?

00:40:56.520 --> 00:40:58.283
You've let your anger
consume you.

00:40:58.355 --> 00:40:59.515
Now it's consuming us.

00:40:59.590 --> 00:41:00.818
She has condemned us all.

00:41:00.891 --> 00:41:02.654
Misery loves company.

00:41:02.726 --> 00:41:04.091
Get away from me!

00:41:04.161 --> 00:41:05.093
Or what?

00:41:05.162 --> 00:41:07.892
You'll kill us where we stand?

00:41:07.965 --> 00:41:10.729
Tell me what you want me to be!

00:41:10.801 --> 00:41:13.326
A good Starfleet officer?

00:41:13.404 --> 00:41:14.894
A good Maquis?

00:41:14.972 --> 00:41:16.906
Lover?

00:41:16.974 --> 00:41:20.171
Daughter?

00:41:20.244 --> 00:41:22.508
Just tell me
what you want from me!

00:41:22.580 --> 00:41:25.378
We don't want anything
from you, B'Elanna.

00:41:25.449 --> 00:41:26.939
We only want you.

00:41:27.017 --> 00:41:28.450
We're not your enemies.

00:41:28.519 --> 00:41:29.918
Defend yourself.

00:41:32.323 --> 00:41:34.917
I don't know how.

00:41:34.992 --> 00:41:37.961
I am so tired of fighting.

00:41:38.095 --> 00:41:39.027
We know.

00:42:01.118 --> 00:42:04.110
You've taken the first step
of your journey.

00:42:05.823 --> 00:42:07.450
And what about you?

00:42:07.525 --> 00:42:10.756
We will see each other again.

00:42:10.828 --> 00:42:14.161
In Sto-Vo-Kor?

00:42:14.231 --> 00:42:17.166
Yes, in Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:42:17.234 --> 00:42:21.500
Or maybe... when you get home.

00:42:26.944 --> 00:42:28.138
Mother?

00:42:40.824 --> 00:42:44.282
Oh, God, I'm alive.

00:42:50.935 --> 00:42:52.664
Welcome back.
